spans.s:
व्य्—अहन् or व्य्—अह्न (loc. ˚ह्नि, ˚हनि, or ˚ह्ने), Pāṇ. vi, 3, 110; Vop. iii, 42;
 (-अह्न), mfn. done or happening on separate days, MW.;
 (accord. to some ‘done or produced in two days’).

व्य्-आ-√ हन् P. -हन्ति, to strike at excessively, strike back, repel, Vas.; BhP.;
to impede, obstruct, fail, disappoint, Kāv.; Sāh.; Suśr. :
Caus. -घातयति, to repel, obstruct, MBh.

व्य्—अहन् or व्य्—अह्न (loc. ˚ह्नि, ˚हनि, or ˚ह्ने), Pāṇ. vi, 3, 110; Vop. iii, 42;
 (-अह्न), mfn. done or happening on separate days, MW.;
 (accord. to some ‘done or produced in two days’).

‘arranger, compiler’, N. of a celebrated mythical sage and author (often called Veda-vyāsa and regarded as the original compiler and arranger of the Vedas, Vedānta-sūtras &c.;
he was the son of the sage Parāśara and Satyavatī, and half-brother of Vicitra-vīrya and Bhīṣma;
he was also called Vādarāyaṇa or Bādarāyaṇa, and Kṛṣṇa from his dark complexion, and Dvaipāyana because he was brought forth by Satyavatī on a Dvīpa or island in the Jumnā;
when grown up he retired to the wilderness to lead the life of a hermit, but at his mother's request returned to become the husband of Vicitra-vīrya's two childless widows, by whom he was the father of the blind Dhṛtarāṣṭra and of Pāṇḍu;
he was also the father of Vidura [q.v.] by a slave girl, and of Śuka, the supposed narrator of the Bhāgavata-Purāṇa, he was also the supposed compiler of the Mahā-bhārata, the Purāṇas, and other portions of Hindū sacred literature;
but the name Vyāsa seems to have been given to any great typical compiler or author), MBh.;
Hariv.;
Pur. cf.

व्य्-√ अञ्ज् P. Ā. -अनक्ति, -अङ्क्ते, (Ā.) to anoint thoroughly, RV.;
to decorate, adorn, beautify, ib.;
 (P. Ā.) to cause to appear, manifest, display, RV. &c. &c.:
Pass. -अज्यते, to be manifested or expressed, RV.; Ragh.; Pañcat. :
Caus. -अञ्जयति, to cause to appear, make clearly visible or manifest, Mn.; MBh. &c.

(अति-√ इ) P. -अत्येति, to pass away, elapse, MBh.; R. &c.;
to take an irregular course, PañcavBr.;
to depart or deviate or swerve from (abl.), R.; Ragh.;
to go past or beyond or through (acc.), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to surpass, overcome, conquer, MBh.;
to disregard, neglect, Bhag.

व्य्-अति-√ क्रम् P. Ā. -क्रामति, -क्रमते (ind.p. -क्रम्य), to go or pass by, step over or beyond (lit. and fig.), MBh.; R.; Pañcat.;
to pass away, elapse, be spent (as time), ib.; BhP.;
to excel, surpass, conquer, R.;
to neglect, omit, violate, ib.

व्य्-अति-√ रिच् Pass. -रिच्यते, to reach far beyond, leave behind, surpass, excel (acc. or abl.), Hariv.; Ragh.;
to be separated from (abl.), BhP.;
to differ from, ib.; Śaṃk.

व्य्-अति-√ वृत् Ā. -वर्तते, to go over, pass through, R.;
to escape, avoid, MBh.;
to glide or pass away, elapse, ib.; R.; Hariv.;
to depart from (abl.), leave, quit, abandon, R.

P. Ā. -षजति, ˚ते, (P.) to join or unite in opposite places, connect mutually, intertwine, TBr.; Uttarar.;
to implicate, involve in (a game), Daś.;
 (Ā.) to change, MW. :
Pass. -षज्यते, to be mutually connected, ib.

cl. 1. Ā. (Dhātup. xix, 2) व्य॑थते (ep. also ˚ति; pf. विव्यथे, 3. pl. ˚थुः, MBh.; aor. व्यथिषि, AV.; Subj. व्यथिषत्, Br.; fut. व्यथिता, ˚थिष्यते Gr.; inf. व्यथितुम्, ib., Ved. inf. व्यथिष्यै),
to tremble, waver, go astray, come to naught, fail, RV. &c. &c. (with abl. = to be deprived of, lose; with चरित्र-तस्, to abandon the path of virtue);
to fall (on the ground), Mn. vii, 84 (‘to be dried up’, Kull.);
to cease, become ineffective (as poison), Kām.;
to be agitated or disturbed in mind, be restless or sorrowful or unhappy, AV. &c. &c.;
to be afraid of (gen.), R. Caus. व्यथ॑यति (aor. विव्यथस्, Br.; व्यथयीस्, AV.),
to cause to tremble or fall, RV. &c. &c.;
to cause to swerve from (abl.), Bhaṭṭ.;
to disquiet, frighten, agitate, pain, afflict, MBh.; Kāv. &c.:
Pass. of Caus. व्यथ्यते, to be set in restless motion, Suśr. :
Desid. विव्यथिषते Gr.:
Intens. वाव्यथ्यते, वाव्यत्ति, ib.

cl. 4. P. (Dhātup. xxvi, 72) वि॑ध्यति (ep. also ˚ते; pf. p. विव्याध, Br. &c.; 3. pl. विव्यधुः, MBh., विविधुः, Up.; Ā. विव्यधे, MBh.; p. विविध्व॑स्, RV.; aor. व्यात्सीः, Br.; Prec. विध्यात् Gr.; fut. वेद्धा, वेत्स्यति, ˚ते, MBh.; व्यद्धा, व्यत्स्यति Gr.; inf. वेद्धुम्, MBh.; -विधे, RV.; ind.p. विद्ध्वा, -विध्य, MBh.),
to pierce, transfix, hit, strike, wound, RV. &c. &c. ;
 (with सिराम्) to open a vein, bleed, Suśr.;
to pelt with (instr.), RV.; AV.; MBh.;
to inflict, attach to, affect with (acc. of pers. and instr. of thing), RV.; AV.; Br.; Up.;
to shake, wave, MBh.;
 (in astron.) to fix the position of a heavenly body, Gol.;
to cling to (acc.), ŚBr. :
Caus. व्याधयति or व्यधयति, (ep. also वेधयति; aor. अवीविधत् or अविव्यधत्),
to pierce, open (a vein), MBh.; Suśr.;
to cause to pierce or perforate, AitĀr. :
Desid. विव्यत्सति, to wish to affect or taint with (instr.), ŚBr. :
Intens. वेविध्यते or वाव्यद्धि (?) Gr.

व्य्-अप-√ कृष् P. -कर्षति, to draw or drag away or off, MBh.; R.;
to lead astray, seduce, MBh.;
to take off (as clothes), undress, ib.;
to take away, remove, give up, abandon, Mn.; MBh. &c.

व्य्-अप-√ नी P. -नयति (inf. -नेतुम्, or -नयितुम्), to lead or take away, MBh.; R.;
to drive away, remove, banish, ib. &c.;
to pour out or away, AitBr.;
to take off, lay aside, get rid of (acc.), MBh.; Kāv. &c.:
Caus. -नाययति, to cause to take away or remove, MBh.

व्य्-अप-√ रुह् Caus. -रोपयति, to lay aside, remove, take off, R.;
to deprive of, expel from (instr. or abl.), MBh.;
to root up, eradicate, extirpate (see next).

(-अप- √ 1. ऊह्) P. -अपोहति (ep. also ˚ते), to drive away, keep off, remove, destroy, TUp.; Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to atone for, expiate (guilt), Mn. ii, 102 &c.;
to heal, cure (sickness), Suśr.

व्य्-अभि-√ चर् P. Ā. -चरति, to act in an unfriendly way towards (acc. or gen.), sin against, offend, injure, MBh. : Kathās.;
to bewitch, practise sorcery (pl. ‘against each other’), Lāṭy.; Kathās.;
to come to naught, fail, Bījag.; BhP.;
to go beyond, transgress, deviate from (acc.), Kir.; Pāṇ., Sch.

1. व्यय् cl. 1. P. Ā. व्ययति, ˚ते (rather Nom. fr. व्यय below), to expend, spend, waste, Bhaṭṭ.; Hit.; Subh.;
 cl. 10. P. व्यययति id., Dhātup. xxxv, 78;
to go, move, ib.

व्य्-√ अर्द् P. -अर्दति, to flow away, ŚBr.;
to oppress, harass, pain (see अ-व्यर्ण) :
Caus. -अर्दयति, to cause to be scattered or dissolved, destroy, annihilate, RV.

P. -च्छिनत्ति, to cut off, separate, ŚBr.; MBh. &c.;
to tear asunder, open, sunder, R.; BhP.;
to limit, fix, settle, ascertain, BhP.;
to resolve on (प्रति), ib. :
Pass. -च्छिद्यते, to be cut off or separated, ŚBr.

व्य्-अव-√ धा P. Ā. -दधाति, -द्कत्ते, to place apart or asunder, ŚāṅkhBr.;
to put or place between, interpose, Ragh.;
to leave out, omit, Kāṭh.;
to separate, divide, interrupt, BhP. :
Pass. -धीयते, to be separated or divided or interrupted, R.; BhP. :
Caus., -धापयति, to separate, Naiṣ.

व्य्-अव-√ धू P. Ā. -धूनोति, ˚नुते, to shake off, ward off, remove, Kāṭh.; Hariv.; R.;
to shake about, treat roughly or rudely, MBh.;
to reject, repel, ib.

व्य्-अव-√ सृज् P. Ā. -सृजति, ˚ते, to throw, cast, hurl upon (gen.), MBh.;
to put or lay down, ib.;
to dismiss, send away, ŚBr.;
to distribute, bestow (see व्य्-अवसर्ग),
to hang on, fasten to (loc.), MBh. viii, 959 (prob. w.r. for व्यव-√ सञ्ज्).

व्य्-अव-√ सो P. -स्यति (ep. also -स्यते [with act. and pass. meaning]; 1. sg. pr. -सामि; Pot. -सेयम्, -सेत्; fut. -सिष्यति),
to settle down or dwell separately, ŚBr.;
to differ (in opinion), contest, quarrel, ib.;
to separate, divide (opp. to सम्-√ अस्), RPrāt.;
to determine, resolve, decide, be willing to (acc. dat., अर्थम् ifc., or inf.), TBr. &c. &c.;
to settle, ascertain, be convinced or persuaded of, take for (acc.), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to ponder, reflect, consider, MBh.; Śak.;
to make strenuous effort, labour or seek after, make an attempt upon (acc.), MW. :
Pass. -सीयते, to be settled or ascertained or fixed on or determined or decided (often impers.), MBh.; Kāv. &c.:
Caus. -साययति, to cause to resolve, encourage to undertake, embolden, VS.; TS. ;
to incite or instigate to (inf.), Kir.

व्य्-अव-√ स्था Ā. -तिष्ठते, to go apart, separate from (abl.), ŚāṅkhŚr.;
to differ respectively, Śaṃk.;
to halt, stop, stay, R.;
to prepare or make ready for (dat.), ib.;
to be settled, be (logically) true or tenable, MBh.; Sarvad.;
to appear as (nom.), Nir.; Sāṃkhyak. :
Caus. -स्थापयति, to put down, place, VarBṛS.; Vās.;
to fix on, direct towards (loc.), Kum.;
to charge with, appoint to (अर्थम्), Hit.;
to stop, hold up, prevent from falling, MBh.; Rājat.;
to restore, re-establish, Kum.; Jātakam.;
to settle, arrange, establish, determine, prove to be (logically) tenable, Daś.; Sarvad.;
to give a name, Divyāv.;
to perform, MW.

व्य्-अव-√ हृ P. Ā. -हरति, ˚ते, to transpose, exchange, Nir.;
to have intercourse with (instr. or loc.), GṛS.; BhP.;
to meet (as foes), fight with (instr. with or without सार्धम्), MBh. to act, proceed, behave towards or deal with (loc.), ib.; Kāv. &c.;
to be active or busy, work, Yājñ., Sch.;
to carry on commerce, trade, deal in (loc. instr., or gen.), Āpast.; VarBṛS.; BhP.;
to bet at, play for (gen.), Pāṇ. ii, 3, 57, Sch.;
to manage, employ make use of (acc.), ib.;
to carry on legal proceedings, litigate, MW.;
to be intent upon, care for cherish (acc.), MBh.;
to roam or stroll about, ib.;
to recover, regain, obtain, ib.;
to distinguish, ib. Pass. -ह्रियते, to be named or termed or designated, Sarvad.; Vedāntas. :
Caus. -हारयति, to allow any one to do what he likes, Kull. on Mn. viii, 362 to deal with (acc.), SaddhP. :
Pass. of Caus. हार्यते, to be named or designated, BhP.

(-अव-√ इ) P. -अवौति, to go or pass between, separate, ŚBr.; Kauś.;
 (in gram.) to resolve or separate by inserting a vowel, Prāt.;
to dissolve, decompose, MW.

व्य्-√ अश् P. Ā. -अश्नोति, -अश्नुते, to reach, attain, Bhaṭṭ.;
to obtain, take possession of RV.; AV.; ŚBr.; ĀśvŚr.;
to fall to one's share, RV.; AV.;
to pervade, interpenetrate, fill, occupy, Ragh.; Bhaṭṭ.

व्य्-√ 2. अस् अस् P. -अस्यति (ep. pf. विव्यास as if fr. a √ व्यस्), to throw or cast asunder or about or away, throw (effort) into, divide, separate, dispose, arrange ;
 scatter, disperse;
 expel, remove, RV. &c. &c.

व्य्-आ-√ कृ P. Ā. -करोति, -कुरुते, to undo, sever, divide, separate from (instr.), RV.; AV.; VS.; ŚBr.;
to expound, explain, declare, MBh.; R.;
 (with Buddhists) to predict (esp. future births), Divyāv.;
to prophesy anything (acc.) about any one (acc.), Lalit.; Kāraṇḍ.;
 Pass. -क्रियते, to be divided or separated, ŚBr.

व्य्-आ-√ क्षिप् P. Ā. -क्षिपति, ˚ते, to stretch out (the hand &c.), MBh.;
to shoot off (an arrow), ib.;
to carry away, captivate (the mind), R.; Pañcat.

व्य्-आ-√ ख्या P. -ख्याति, to explain in detail, tell in full, discuss, ŚBr.; ŚrS.;
to relate, communicate, MBh.; Bhaṭṭ.;
to name, call, Śrutab. Desid. -चिख्यासति, to wish to explain, Śaṃk.

2. व्य्-आ-√ दिश् P. -दिशति, to point out separately, divide among, distribute, TS. &c. &c.;
to point out, show, explain, teach, R.; Prab.;
to prescribe, enjoin, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to appoint, assign, despatch to any place or duty, direct, order, command (with dat. loc., or प्रति), ib.;
to declare, foretell, Mālav. v, 12/13 (v.l. आदिष्टा for व्य्-आद्˚).

व्य्-आ-√ पद् Ā. -पद्यते, to fall away, fall into misfortune, perish, be lost, fail, miscarry, MBh.; Suśr.;
to disappear, be changed into another sound or symbol, RPrāt., Sch. (cf. व्य्-आपन्न) :
Caus. -पादयति, to cause to perish, make worse, injure, hurt, spoil, kill, destroy, MBh.; Kāv. &c.

व्य्-आ-√ यम् P. Ā. -यच्छति, ˚ते, (P.) to pull or drag or draw asunder, extend, Lāṭy.;
to sport or dally with (loc.), Suśr.;
 Ā. (P. only mc.) to struggle or contend about (loc.), fight together, make efforts, strive, endeavour, TS.; Br.; MBh. &c.:
Caus. यामयति or यमयति, to cause to stretch out or struggle, make great effort or exertion, take exercise (ind.p. -याम्य, having taken exercise), Mn. vii, 216.

व्य्-आ-√ वल्ग् P. -वल्गति, to jump about, bound or leap from one place to another, Bālar.;
to gallop, Uttarar.;
to quiver, throb, be agitated (as a bosom), Kuval.

व्य्-आ-√ वृत् Ā. -वर्तते (rarely P.), to become separated or singled out from (instr.), RV.; AV.; Br.;
to become separated or distinct, be distinguished as or in some partic. form of MaitrUp.;
to turn or wind in different directions, divide (as a road), MBh.;
to be dispersed (as an army), Hariv.;
to be opened, Suśr.;
to turn away from, part with, get rid of (instr. or abl.), Ragh.; Kathās.;
to diverge from, be inconsistent with (abl.), Sarvad.;
to go away, depart, Śāntiś.;
to come back, return, Ratnāv.; Rājat.;
to turn round, revolve, R.;
to sink (as the sun), MBh.;
to come to an understanding or settlement, AitBr.;
to come to an end, cease, perish, disappear, MBh.; Hariv. &c.:
Caus. -वर्तयति (Pass. -वर्त्यते), to divide, separate from (instr. or abl.; ind.p. -वर्त्य, ‘with the exception of’, Bālar.), TBr. &c. &c.;
to free from (instr.), MaitrS.;
to turn about or round, MBh.; Kād.;
to keep back, avert, R.;
to throw about, strew, MBh.;
to exchange, substitute one for another, Hariv.;
to lay aside (the staff), R.;
 (with अन्यथा) to retract (a word), MBh.;
to remove (pain or distress), Vikr.;
to destroy or annul (an enemy or a rule), Ragh. xv, 7 :
Desid. -विवृसते, to wish or intend to liberate one's self from or get rid of (abl.), ŚBr.

व्य्-आ-√ सञ्ज् (only 3. du. impf. Ā. व्य्-आ-सजेताम्; and ind.p. -सज्य),
to adhere separately or severally (see comp.);
to begin to fight hand to hand, Śiś. xviii, 12.

व्य्-आ-√ हृ P. Ā. -हरति, ˚ते, to utter or pronounce a sound, speak, say to (acc.), converse with (सह), name (with नामभिस्, to call by name; with प्रश्नान्, to answer questions; with उदाहराणि, to state examples), TBr. &c. &c.;
to begin to talk (said of a child), MBh.;
to confess, avow to (gen.), ib.;
to utter inarticulate sounds, cry, scream (said of animals), KātyŚr.;
to sport, enjoy one's self (exceptionally for वि-√ हृ), BhP.;
to cut off, sever, MBh. vi, 2757 (B. वि-√ हृ) :
Desid. -जिहीर्षति, to wish to pronounce or utter, ŚBr.
